    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Bryce Harper** (72.33) and **Cal Raleigh** (72.28), our two most potent offensive catalysts. **Bryce Harper** draws a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, benefiting from a soft xERA and a solid +6% boost from his projected #3 spot. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** remains a top-tier play; despite a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Jedixson Paez, the sheer weight of the SP\u2019s 9.12 xERA pushes his efficiency score well into the elite tier. Further down the lineup, **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) has surged into \"Strong\" territory, capitalizing on a stellar +14% park factor and a +17% boost from a generous matchup against Gabriel Hughes.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Gleyber Torres**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 46.16. While his projected leadoff role provided a significant +10% boost, the optimizer favored the speed upside and positional utility of our current outfield and middle infield configuration. Specifically, **Zack Gelof** (55.13) earned his spot over the bench options because his matchup against MacKenzie Gore includes a \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric that enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our internal scoring priorities. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (52.25) remains in the lineup despite a subpar SP matchup because his +10% platoon edge against Sean Burke helps maintain our floor in a day where we are monitoring the SB category closely.\n\nWe are currently operating under a \"Lineup Pending\" status for the entire roster, which introduces inherent volatility. Owners should keep a close eye on the official reports, particularly for **Justin Crawford** (54.00); should his confirmed batting order drop lower than the #8 spot, his efficiency score will likely dip below our viable threshold. While the weather looks stable, the aggressive targeting of pitchers like Paez means we are banking heavily on high-upside offensive environments. Ensure that **Tyler Freeman** remains benched as he is currently in the minors, and continue to monitor **Jung Hoo Lee**\u2014his elite sprint speed makes him a potential substitution candidate if any of our starters are scratched or if we find ourselves trailing significantly in the SB category as the afternoon games progress.",
